CU.1.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/main/scala/commitool/infrastructure/environment/DotEnvLoader.scala
CU.1.LABEL=SEVERITY:CRITICAL — Complete the single-quote literal fix: integrate ValueType into the full load pipeline, fix syntax error, remove dead code
CU.1.INSTRUCT=Rewrite DotEnvLoader to properly integrate the ValueType/Expandable/Literal tagging throughout the pipeline. The current v002 code has:
  1. A stray unmatched closing brace on line 66 (syntax error)
  2. envVars is still Map[String, String] — doesn't accept ValueType
  3. resolveExpansions still takes Map[String, String] — never sees the ValueType
  4. Dead code on lines 37-38 (sys.env.foreach discarding results)
  
Make these changes:

  A. Keep the ValueType sealed trait structure (already added correctly in v002):
    private sealed trait ValueType
    private case class Literal(value: String) extends ValueType
    private case class Expandable(value: String) extends ValueType

  B. Fix parseValue — KEEP the existing v002 implementation (it's correct). Remove the stray extra closing brace that was introduced.

  C. Change envVars from Map[String, String] to Map[String, ValueType]:
    val envVars = mutable.Map[String, ValueType]()

  D. Remove the dead sys.env.foreach block after resolveExpansions (currently lines 37-38). System env vars are already loaded before .env processing on line 18.

  E. Change resolveExpansions to accept Map[String, ValueType] and handle the Literal/Expandable distinction:
    private def resolveExpansions(raw: Map[String, ValueType]): Map[String, String]
    
    For each key:
    - If ValueType is Literal(value) -> return value as-is, no expansion
    - If ValueType is Expandable(value) -> apply varExpansionRegex replacement (same logic as current expandVar)
    
    Implementation approach:
    1. Separate into literalVars and expandableVars
    2. Resolve expansions on expandableVars only (same recursive resolution with depth/cycle detection)
    3. Merge literalVars with expanded expandableVars
    4. Return Map[String, String]

  F. Ensure the final return type of load() is still Map[String, String] — the resolved types are String.

  G. Verify the file compiles with sbt compile before submitting.

